    Bug 1806770 - Split nsIMsgDatabase.createNewHdr() into two separate functions to make discouraged variation more obvious and painful. r=mkmelin

    This splits the old nsIMsgDatabase.createNewHdr() method into two separate variants:
    The common path is .createNewHdr(), which longer takes a nsMsgKey param as the database assigns one.
    The discouraged path is now .createNewHdrWithSpecificMsgKey() which forces the DB to use the given nsMsgKey.
    Previously this behaviour was decided by the passed key being nsMsgKey_None.
    Because the key was often being passed down through multiple layers, this made things hard to track.
    This change should make it more obvious where the IMAP UID is being force-fed as the local database key.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D305082

